---
// How a template pack gets into ViewSwitcher, and which version can install one (PACK_INSTALL_VERSION).
import { site } from "../site.config";
const v = site.packInstallVersion;
---
<ol class="install">
  <li>Download the template pack (a .zip).</li>
  <li>In ViewSwitcher, open <strong>Templates</strong>.</li>
  <li>Drop the .zip anywhere on that page. You'll see every view before anything is added.</li>
  <li>Press <strong>Install</strong>. The pack becomes its own template set, beside your own templates.</li>
  <li>Make a scene from one of its views and retype the names and titles right on the view.</li>
</ol>
<p class="needs">{v
  ? <>Installing template packs needs ViewSwitcher {v} or later. It updates itself.</>
  : <>Installing template packs comes in the next ViewSwitcher update. ViewSwitcher updates itself, so you'll have it as soon as it's out.</>}</p>
<style>
  .install { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.45rem; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 44rem; }
  .install strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .needs { color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 0.9375rem; max-width: 44rem; }
</style>
